WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.800
Step five plans against the
fictional tenant, sending nothing.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.575
The check passes again, and
the plan has three Blocked,

3
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:11.950
four Create, one NoChange, one
NotInRepository and two Update.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.187
The dry run writes six
requests and sends none.

5
00:00:15.187 --> 00:00:16.313
Look at the list.

6
00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:19.637
Context C one is created
and C two updated.

7
00:00:19.637 --> 00:00:22.662
The privileged authentication
strength is created.

8
00:00:22.662 --> 00:00:27.351
Two policies are created, and the
compliant-device policy is updated.

9
00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:32.589
Three are Blocked: C A oh oh three, because
the strength it needs doesn't exist yet,

10
00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:36.378
and the two context policies,
the activation gate and the

11
00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:40.650
protected actions policy, because
C one doesn't exist yet either.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.222
And C A oh oh one, the
legacy authentication block,

13
00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:46.812
is in the tenant but not in the files.

14
00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:50.400
It's reported as NotInRepository,
and never deleted.
